# EA1-only kernel config, on top of board/ea/common/linux/common.fragment.
# Reachability is Wi-Fi (AR9485, mainline ath9k); the EA3 has no radio.

# --- kernel command line (EA1) ---
# pci=realloc,nocrs is REQUIRED: CEFDK leaves the ath9k/e1000 BARs unassigned and
# this is the combination proven to bring up wlan0. Do NOT copy to another board
# without checking its E820 (see the EA3 fragment, where `nocrs` breaks the NIC).
# pci=routeirq enables the CE5300 UART interrupt link (LUAR/GSI 38) for the IO-MCU
# on ttyS1 — see board/ea/common/linux/common.fragment.
#
# The RAM reclaim (memmap=exactmap, which brings MemTotal from ~176 MB to ~1.7 GB
# — PROVEN on this EA1) is NOT here: the EA1 boots through the S00kexec bootstrap,
# whose kexec --command-line replaces CONFIG_CMDLINE, so a memmap set here would
# never reach the real kernel. It lives in board.env's OHC_KEXEC_CMDLINE_EXTRA,
# which S00kexec appends. (The EA3 boots direct, so its reclaim IS in its fragment
# CONFIG_CMDLINE — see ea3-v2.fragment for the full per-entry derivation.)
CONFIG_CMDLINE="console=ttyS0,115200 earlyprintk=serial,ttyS0,115200 pci=realloc,nocrs,routeirq"
